  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> is a root of the quadratic equation <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>–</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>–</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>–</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In given equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>And, we know that the irrational roots of a quadratic equation exist in conjugate pair, if the coefficients are rational.</p><p>Thus,&nbsp;if one root of the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then, the other root will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>We know that the sum and product of the roots of a quadratic equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are respectively&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Therefore, the sum of roots&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>p</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>And, the product of roots&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Thus, the answer is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
